MEMLEAKPROBE(1)

NAME
    memleakprobe - test kernel memory drift under common workloads

SYNOPSIS
    memleakprobe

DESCRIPTION
    Runs repeated fork/wait, pipe, file, mmap/munmap, and socket create/close
    workloads while sampling sys_meminfo before and after the run.

    The probe reports PASS only when the workload succeeds and PMM/kalloc
    accounting returns to baseline within the documented probe tolerance.

NOTES
    This is primarily a diagnostic or self-test helper, but it is documented so installed programs are discoverable.
